From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sproutboat <noreply@sproutboat.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] render: collector hooks for the fork template (quiet, seal,
 immortal pages, memory limit)

sproutd's collector hooks. porf_gc_quiet is idle collection on demand; porf_gc_seal_heap closes every
open allocation window, drops the partial-page lists and seals every page the template filled before
it forks, so a child allocates into fresh pages instead of copy-on-write copies of the template's.
A sealed page is immortal in the worker: a worker's full collection neither clears nor sets its mark
bits nor sweeps it, and what a template object comes to reference in the worker is found through the
card table (cards below the template top are never cleared). Without this every worker's first full
collection rewrote the metadata of the whole template heap (56 KiB per worker on a 1.5 MiB template).

porf_gc_set_limit(bytes) lets the host pass the app's memory limit to the collector (plan 001 step B):
the nursery and the budget are clamped to half of what the limit leaves above what is live, never
below 1 MiB. Unset (0): upstream's own pacing.

Class: ours
Pass: patchGcHooks
---
